  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5751e45b3bc551448917ed569792a2a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 19
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  fullText: 'The temperature is getting unbearable. We are being forced to retreat
    deeper and deeper as the water\nevaporates at unbelievable speeds. Proima has
    never lived through something like this before. No\nnatural disaster that ever
    hit our planet can compare to this catastrophe.                                                                                                                                                                             
    \n\nIt has been months of hard work, yet all the research I have done has proven
    useless. After every dead\nend I see my colleagues grow more tired and hopeless.
    At this point, no scientific advances are being\nmade; I just sit in the lab,
    my mind wandering.                                                                                                                                                                             
    \n\nLast week, I caught myself thinking about how to restore the planet when
    we lose to the invaders, but I\nfigured I was being pessimistic by assuming defeat.
    Now I know I was actually being optimistic, thinking\nafter all this passes there
    would be anyone left to do the restoring.                                                                                                                                                                             
    \n\nAs I write this lines I don''t know how or where you are. Although everything
    is looking grimmer and\ngrimmer for the Povann, I would be happy just knowing
    that you alone are okay. That you are still able to\nlive the last years of your
    life peacefully as you have always wanted. I try to hold on to the idea that
    you\nwill read this in some safe, secluded place, but I am starting to think
    such a thing does not exist.                                                                                                                                                                             
    \n\nI miss you mom. I am scared.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              '
